# save: 36-CavePast
# The end of the Giygas fight: Pokey and Giygas's second form are set to 1 HP in the setup
# (`ehp`; the setup seeds the RNG before each round so both sides play the same rounds, and
# `heal` stops the rolling meters), which reaches the prayer phase. The body plays the prayers
# (Paula Prays; Ness Defends, or casts Healing gamma on Paula when Giygas's flash knocked her
# out; Jeff and Poo Defend), the player's prayer and Giygas's death, to the battle's end.
# Body generated from a port run with playtest/padlog_body.py.
# The battle's effects run over budget nearly every frame in the original (giygas.play)
# overclock: max
# Returning from a prayer's vignette, LOAD_BATTLE_SCENE's FADE_IN follows the load lag: the
# original's fade-in ends a logic frame later (NMI-driven; battle-autowin.play) and that extra
# WAIT_FOR_FADE_WITH_TICK frame ticks a window (RAND), so the RNGs end one call apart. A
# `# lag:` per such fade lines the frames up again, and a `# reseed:` right after it re-seeds
# both sides before the next turn's initiative rolls. Each vignette's TELEPORT load: the first
# emu sample is part-way in (skip), its SCREEN_TRANSITION takes one more frame (lag)
# The body stops at the battle's end: the original's HP meters roll differently there (lag
# frames), so @WAIT_HPPP_STABLE ticks once more and everything after is a frame off
